# Neon Data API + Neon Auth — both PUBLIC by design (they're the browser's
# entry points, protected by RLS + the auth token, not by secrecy). Never
# put a Postgres connection string, a Meta token, or the svc_sync password
# in this file or anywhere under web/ — see web/README.md "Sécurité".
#
# IMPORTANT — URL trap, see web/README.md "Piège de l'URL Data API":
# the Neon console shows a LONG url like
#   https://ep-xxx.apirest.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb/rest/v1
# Strip ".apirest" from the hostname AND the trailing "/rest/v1" before
# using it here. The short form:
#   https://ep-xxx.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb
# Both variables below normally take this SAME short base URL — the SDK
# derives the actual Data API and Auth endpoints from it. Only use a
# different value for VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL if the Neon console's Auth tab
# explicitly shows you a different one.

VITE_NEON_DATA_API_URL=
VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL=
